EVALUATION.md §1, TYPES.md §1: a type error in one let and an unknown name in one fn break those
declarations and their readers only. `readsBad` and `callsBad` produce no evaluation finding;
`div` is still evaluated (E4102), `big` still checked (E5001), and so is the value of the
imported package that `viaFine` reads, while `viaBroken` reads a broken import and stays silent.
-- check-only --
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
}
-- b/b.canon --
/// B.
package b

/// Broken in the import.
let broken: Int = true

/// Divides by zero when read.
let fine: Int = 1 / 0
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

import b

/// Slot.
record Slot {
  /// Size.
  size: Int

  check fits: size < 10 else "too big"
}

/// Type error.
let bad: Int = "nope"

/// Reads the broken let: broken too, never evaluated.
let readsBad: Int = bad / 0

/// Unknown name.
fn badFn(x: Int) -> Int { return x + unknownName }

/// Calls the broken fn: broken too, never evaluated.
let callsBad: Int = badFn(2) / 0

/// Unrelated: still evaluated.
let div: Int = 1 / 0

/// Unrelated: still checked.
let big: Slot = { size: 30 }

/// Reads a broken value of an import: never evaluated.
let viaBroken: Int = b.broken / 0

/// Reads a sound value of an import: evaluated.
let viaFine: Int = b.fine
-- select --
a
-- findings.txt --
error[E3002]  a/a.canon:15:16
  expected Int, found String

error[E2102]  a/a.canon:21:38
  unknown name unknownName

error[E4102]  a/a.canon:27:16
  div: division by zero

error[E5001]  a/a.canon:30:17
  big: too big
  expected by a/a.canon:11 (check fits)

error[E3002]  b/b.canon:5:19
  expected Int, found Bool

error[E4102]  b/b.canon:8:17
  fine: division by zero

6 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
